  "scope": "generalized_identity assumes nonnegative coordinates of x and strictly positive coordinates of y, with no mass constraint. It proves differentiability of entropy at y and the divergence formula with its mass correction. simplex_identity further assumes both vectors have mass one. interior_lower_bound assumes both vectors have strictly positive coordinates and both masses are one, giving half the squared l1 distance as a lower bound for finiteKL. binary_boundary establishes continuity, the two endpoint values log 2, agreement with finiteKL, and the quadratic lower bound on [0,1] for reference 1/2. scaled_binary_use assumes real t and s with 1 ≤ t and |s| ≤ t, including equality |s| = t. The three consumers cover unequal mass with zero numerator, quarter interior, and endpoints with scaling.",
